<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mutomboko</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mutomboko ceremony</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mutomboko is an annual ceremony of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lunda-empire">Lunda</a> people of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luapula-river">Luapula</a> valley in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zambia">Zambia</a>, held each July at Mwansabombwe, the seat of the Mwata <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kazembe">Kazembe</a>. It commemorates the Lunda migration from the kingdom of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mwata-yamvo">Mwata Yamvo</a> and the conquest of the Luapula valley in the 18th century, and it culminates in a victory dance performed by the Kazembe himself.</p></div>
